repository-code: "https://github.com/CSU-Agricultural-Water-Quality-Program/3d-flume-uncertainty-analysis"
url: "https://github.com/CSU-Agricultural-Water-Quality-Program/3d-flume-uncertainty-analysis"
abstract: >-
  R scripts and calibration data for hierarchical Bayesian estimation of
  stage-discharge relationships for two 3D-printed trapezoidal flumes and a
  fiberglass reference flume. The main workflow uses stage in meters and
  discharge in liters per second, propagates point-gauge uncertainty through
  latent stage, and estimates proportional and additive discharge uncertainty.
  Supporting scripts generate sampler diagnostics, rating-curve figures,
  uncertainty-component plots, prediction tables, and manuscript summaries.
  Historical scripts and calibration outputs are retained separately.
keywords:
  - Bayesian calibration
  - stage-discharge relationship
  - trapezoidal flume
  - agricultural water measurement
  - measurement uncertainty
  - 3D printing
  - R
